WEBVTT

00:24.230 --> 00:26.830
Papa Rei? G'morning.

00:26.830 --> 00:27.840
Good morning.

00:27.840 --> 00:29.950
Are you going out?

00:29.950 --> 00:33.040
I had to go pee.

00:33.040 --> 00:34.310
I'm heading home for a while.

00:35.900 --> 00:38.500
But your home is here.

00:38.790 --> 00:39.930
True.

00:43.850 --> 00:46.070
Keep it down, you guys.

00:47.160 --> 00:49.720
Huh? Did we have a job today?

00:50.060 --> 00:51.150
No.

00:51.150 --> 00:54.170
Come home soon, Papa Rei!

00:54.170 --> 00:55.250
Today we're gonna—

00:55.250 --> 00:56.190
Hey, Miri!

00:58.170 --> 00:59.400
Shh!

01:01.110 --> 01:03.670
Don't stay out too late, okay?

01:04.260 --> 01:06.670
Have a good day!

01:12.330 --> 01:14.970
Where'd he say he was going?

01:14.970 --> 01:16.780
Home, he said.

01:16.780 --> 01:17.810
Home?

01:21.020 --> 01:23.360
His dad called him home, huh?

01:25.580 --> 01:28.690
Well, saves us the trouble of 
getting him out of the house.

01:29.510 --> 01:32.740
Okay, Miri! Mission start!

01:33.060 --> 01:35.480
Start!

01:38.360 --> 01:41.910
<i>Hey, I want to love, is this true love?</i>

01:41.910 --> 01:45.540
<i>Is just wanting to be loved insincere?</i>

01:45.540 --> 01:47.790
<i>What should I do?</i>

01:47.790 --> 01:50.170
<i>Oh, what should I do?</i>

01:53.460 --> 01:56.470
<i>As usual, the whole city</i>

01:56.470 --> 02:00.140
<i>Is madly in love and excited</i>

02:00.140 --> 02:03.680
<i>Extras like me just go home</i>

02:03.680 --> 02:06.980
<i>But I'm not sulking at all</i>

02:06.980 --> 02:10.810
<i>"And then you appeared suddenly</i>

02:10.810 --> 02:14.360
<i>As though you were ripping 
through those days</i>

02:14.360 --> 02:17.950
<i>With your smile that leaves me numb</i>

02:17.950 --> 02:22.280
<i>You shattered my heart</i>

02:23.450 --> 02:27.040
<i>Hey, I want to love, is this true love?</i>

02:27.040 --> 02:30.670
<i>Is just wanting to be loved insincere?</i>

02:30.670 --> 02:32.840
<i>What should I do?</i>

02:32.840 --> 02:35.170
<i>Oh, what should I do?</i>

02:35.460 --> 02:37.550
<i>How the heck should I know?</i>

02:37.550 --> 02:41.390
<i>I don't know what's going on in your head</i>

02:41.390 --> 02:45.060
<i>But it's not fair that you're so friendly</i>

02:45.060 --> 02:49.770
<i>Once again, I'm being 
swallowed up by your rhythm</i>

02:51.940 --> 02:56.610
<i>There you go, you've got me 
wrapped around your finger again</i>

03:02.910 --> 03:07.790
<i>There you go, you've got me 
wrapped around your finger again</i>

03:52.920 --> 03:54.600
Three years, huh?

03:57.620 --> 04:00.250
Does Papa Rei have two homes?

04:00.260 --> 04:04.510
Spray Whip

04:00.260 --> 04:04.510
Sweetened Whipped Cream

04:00.260 --> 04:04.510
Fresh Whipping Cream

04:00.260 --> 04:04.510
Hoi-Hoi Whip

04:00.260 --> 04:04.510
<b>Light and (sweetened)</b>

04:00.260 --> 04:04.510
<b>Decorate sweet treats!
Sweetened light and fluffy whip!</b>

04:00.260 --> 04:04.510
<b>Delicious richness and flavor</b>

04:00.260 --> 04:04.510
<b>Keep refrigerated</b>

04:00.260 --> 04:04.510
<b>Already Whipped</b>

04:00.260 --> 04:04.510
<b>Less sweet 

Hoi-Hoi
 Whip

Easy Squeeze</b>

04:00.260 --> 04:04.510
<b>Less sweet 

Hoi-Hoi
 Whip

Easy Squeeze</b>

04:00.640 --> 04:04.500
Yeah, there's the house he 
lived in with his dad before.

04:04.500 --> 04:06.540
Papa Rei's papa?

04:06.990 --> 04:08.220
Grandpapa?!

04:08.220 --> 04:11.360
I guess that's what he'd be, sure.

04:11.360 --> 04:13.200
I wanna meet him!

04:13.200 --> 04:14.620
Sorry, can't.

04:14.620 --> 04:16.030
How come?

04:16.030 --> 04:19.100
Rei's dad is one diabolical dude.

04:19.100 --> 04:20.660
Dia-bo-lical?

04:20.660 --> 04:22.550
It's like scary.

04:22.550 --> 04:23.820
Oh!

04:23.820 --> 04:29.070
Hey, when Miss Anna teaches 
us a song, it's diabolical!

04:29.300 --> 04:33.510
Close your hands! Open your hands!

04:34.150 --> 04:37.320
N-Not quite in the same way.

04:58.040 --> 05:00.050
Forgive my long absence, Boss.

05:00.480 --> 05:01.840
You seem well.

05:01.840 --> 05:04.870
So, living among the little people 
has taught you proper etiquette?

05:05.880 --> 05:07.980
Kurusu Kazuki, was it?

05:08.420 --> 05:11.860
He's a peasant, but I see 
he's not entirely useless.

05:13.570 --> 05:16.410
Still, his skills seem poor.

05:16.410 --> 05:21.330
Is he the reason for the numerous 
mistakes on your recent jobs?

05:24.330 --> 05:25.680
The time may have come.

05:28.300 --> 05:30.310
Return to this home.

05:33.450 --> 05:37.060
So is Grandpapa mad at Papa Rei?

05:38.560 --> 05:40.930
Did they get into a fight, maybe?

05:42.370 --> 05:45.930
I think it goes a little deeper than that.

05:45.930 --> 05:48.880
His family's got kind of 
special circumstances.

05:48.880 --> 05:49.820
Cir-cum-stan-ces?

05:49.820 --> 05:53.260
Yeah, Rei's dad really 
expected the world from him.

05:53.260 --> 05:56.930
He was super strict teaching 
him the family business.

05:57.530 --> 06:01.040
So around the time I first met him...

06:04.360 --> 06:07.420
He was sorta like a robot.

06:07.690 --> 06:08.750
A robot?!

06:08.750 --> 06:11.310
Did he combine? Did he shoot beams?!

06:11.820 --> 06:13.940
I don't... think so.

06:13.940 --> 06:16.430
Aw. No beams?

06:18.750 --> 06:24.950
I guess rebelling against his dad was 
part of the reason he left home.

06:25.230 --> 06:29.190
You think Papa Rei can 
make up with Grandpapa?

06:29.710 --> 06:33.190
Huh? Hmm, not sure...

06:33.770 --> 06:38.050
If he did, I wonder if he'd go back.

06:39.610 --> 06:43.100
The blood of the Suwa family 
is the blood of assassins.

06:43.100 --> 06:46.200
Among those who make their living in death,

06:46.200 --> 06:49.050
it could even be considered noble blood.

06:50.220 --> 06:53.320
Wherever there is light, 
darkness inevitably arises.

06:53.320 --> 06:59.040
Those who shine brightest require 
the aid of the deepest darkness.

06:59.720 --> 07:03.290
The Suwa family is the pinnacle 
of that darkness, its sovereign.

07:03.290 --> 07:07.150
And that blood flows through 
your veins as well.

07:07.960 --> 07:09.530
Carry on the family.

07:09.530 --> 07:12.820
That is the reason for your existence.

07:12.820 --> 07:15.280
That's what I raised you to do.

07:17.040 --> 07:19.700
I've given you more than enough leash.

07:19.700 --> 07:25.300
It's time for you to learn the business 
of being head of the organization.

07:26.680 --> 07:27.960
You don't like that?

07:28.990 --> 07:31.920
The reason I allowed you 
to live on the outside

07:31.920 --> 07:34.100
was because of the oath you 
took to return one day.

07:34.500 --> 07:36.110
Yes, sir.

07:36.560 --> 07:39.300
Did you find true belonging on the outside?

07:40.350 --> 07:41.570
No...

07:41.890 --> 07:45.320
You belong here with us.

07:46.870 --> 07:49.660
It seems you've formed pointless ties.

07:50.750 --> 07:54.230
Bad influences are common 
enough in our business.

07:54.230 --> 07:56.440
If one such influence has sullied 
the Suwa family blood—

07:56.440 --> 07:57.480
No.

07:57.480 --> 07:59.680
Kazuki has nothing to do with this.

08:03.280 --> 08:04.990
Please, give me time.

08:06.020 --> 08:08.570
Need to tie up your affairs?

08:10.280 --> 08:12.030
Finish this before the day is over.

08:15.050 --> 08:16.550
I know this man.

08:16.550 --> 08:18.920
He betrayed the organization.

08:18.920 --> 08:21.950
You'd better not betray my expectations.

08:22.980 --> 08:24.560
Yes, Boss.

08:24.560 --> 08:26.560
<b>Weather: Rain
\hLocation: Downtown</b>

08:24.560 --> 08:26.560
<b>Weather: Cloudy
\hLocation: Highway
\h Car A(BMV)
\h\h\hheading for</b>

08:27.010 --> 08:29.560
Huh? You're gonna be late?

08:29.560 --> 08:30.740
<i>Sorry.</i>

08:30.740 --> 08:33.310
We've kinda got stuff planned here!

08:31.100 --> 08:33.310
I wanna talk!

08:33.310 --> 08:34.400
Sorry.

08:34.400 --> 08:35.820
<i>Papa Rei!</i>

08:36.160 --> 08:38.620
<i>You finished your talk with your dad, right?</i>

08:37.580 --> 08:40.870
<i>Phone! I want the phone!</i>

08:39.880 --> 08:42.630
<i>Hello! Am I being heard?</i>

08:42.620 --> 08:44.040
<i>Phone!</i>

08:44.060 --> 08:44.830
Sorry.

08:44.830 --> 08:48.960
Hey! Hey! I wanna talk!

08:46.030 --> 08:48.960
Could you say something other than "sorry"?

08:48.960 --> 08:51.250
Don't hog it, Papa Kazuki!

08:51.250 --> 08:52.950
Papa Rei!

08:52.950 --> 08:54.560
Darn it!

08:54.560 --> 08:57.360
Just be back by dinner!

08:57.360 --> 08:59.010
<i>I'm not sure—</i>

08:59.010 --> 09:00.020
We got pizza and fries!

08:59.430 --> 09:00.940
Wait, hey!

09:00.020 --> 09:01.670
And ca—

09:02.280 --> 09:04.580
We'll be here! See you!

09:06.500 --> 09:09.770
Sheesh. He won't tell me a single 
damn thing that matters.

09:11.150 --> 09:13.650
Papa Kazuki! It made the ding!

09:14.080 --> 09:17.320
Hey, girl! No touching. It's hot.

09:27.830 --> 09:31.010
So you're the heir to the great Suwa family?

09:31.010 --> 09:31.700
Get in.

09:45.980 --> 09:49.230
<b>Weather: Rain
\hLocation: Downtown</b>

09:47.920 --> 09:49.220
That man.

09:49.890 --> 09:52.690
You worked with him previously, I'm told?

09:53.590 --> 09:56.790
He taught me how to use various weapons.

09:57.270 --> 09:59.340
And how to do the job.

09:59.340 --> 09:59.790
Why—

09:59.790 --> 10:02.110
"Why did he betray the organization?"

10:04.380 --> 10:06.700
A pointless question.

10:06.700 --> 10:10.040
You should spend your 
mental energy elsewhere.

10:14.210 --> 10:16.220
<b>Weather: Sunny
Place: In Town

Kaji spotted on a date
 with a woman believed
 to be his wife.</b>

10:16.550 --> 10:18.480
Is this the reason?

10:22.200 --> 10:27.070
He can wait all he likes, 
but she won't be there.

10:29.770 --> 10:31.950
Why do you kill?

10:33.040 --> 10:34.990
For the Suwa family?

10:34.990 --> 10:36.730
For fun?

10:37.790 --> 10:38.990
What about you?

10:39.990 --> 10:41.730
For the concept.

10:42.030 --> 10:43.350
Concept?

10:43.350 --> 10:46.250
A car exists to be driven.

10:46.250 --> 10:49.250
Money exists to put form to desire.

10:49.670 --> 10:51.880
Guns exist to inflict violence.

10:53.570 --> 10:56.880
So what does he exist for?

10:57.820 --> 11:00.530
I look through the materials 
and I wonder these things.

11:01.040 --> 11:03.830
"What is this person's reason for being?"

11:03.830 --> 11:07.920
"What will he see as his life 
passes before his eyes?"

11:07.920 --> 11:11.190
"What's the thing he cares 
about more than anything?"

11:11.190 --> 11:13.140
I speculate on the answers.

11:13.980 --> 11:16.910
Killing is a way of checking those answers.

11:18.300 --> 11:20.150
Distasteful.

11:41.970 --> 11:43.750
I have a favor to ask.

11:44.440 --> 11:47.880
Tell me what he says just before he dies.

11:49.360 --> 11:53.220
I collect last words.

11:53.660 --> 11:56.980
I'd like to record his next to hers.

12:19.620 --> 12:21.710
So you were the one following me?

12:21.710 --> 12:23.260
How appropriate.

12:24.040 --> 12:25.800
I'm here on a job.

12:28.490 --> 12:29.660
Where is she?

12:31.510 --> 12:32.940
I see.

12:34.060 --> 12:38.700
Maybe if the boss loses you, 
he'll understand a bit of how I feel?

12:39.520 --> 12:41.210
No, probably not.

12:42.210 --> 12:44.990
Well, let's see how you do.

12:56.390 --> 12:59.380
Did your father tell you to 
come back to the organization?

13:00.510 --> 13:02.150
When you said you were leaving,

13:02.150 --> 13:04.580
it really raised my estimation of you.

13:04.580 --> 13:07.320
But I guess you're a Suwa 
through and through.

13:38.850 --> 13:41.800
Papa Rei just looks sad sometimes.

13:41.800 --> 13:45.050
Nah, he's just got one of those faces.

13:45.460 --> 13:48.810
Men are such a mystery.

13:48.810 --> 13:52.100
Where'd you learn that phrase?

13:52.100 --> 13:57.940
Sometimes Mama would be drinking 
and she'd look happy but also sad.

13:58.470 --> 14:00.060
Papa Rei's the same.

14:00.060 --> 14:04.730
He looked all snappy today, 
but he also looked sad.

14:14.490 --> 14:17.720
That's why we're doing the party today.

14:17.720 --> 14:22.970
We got all his favorite foods 
to make him feel surprised.

14:23.750 --> 14:27.140
You think he'll smile today?

14:27.770 --> 14:29.510
Yeah, I bet he will.

14:31.800 --> 14:35.220
But when's he coming back?!

15:02.050 --> 15:03.880
Reminds me of old times.

15:03.880 --> 15:06.090
I never once beat you back then.

15:12.210 --> 15:14.320
Acting as a mindless killing tool,

15:14.320 --> 15:16.340
following the organization blindly,

15:16.340 --> 15:19.050
not hesitating to turn 
your blade on anyone...

15:19.470 --> 15:21.480
You're truly the perfect assassin!

15:22.710 --> 15:24.660
That's the law of the organization.

15:24.660 --> 15:26.700
You know you can't ever leave it!

15:28.680 --> 15:30.500
Of course a puppet wouldn't understand.

15:30.810 --> 15:32.810
I found something worth protecting,

15:33.140 --> 15:35.190
so I changed how I live!

15:35.190 --> 15:36.170
That's it!

15:37.060 --> 15:41.040
But you people stole the thing 
I care about more than anything!

16:02.440 --> 16:06.550
I have something worth protecting, too.

16:08.390 --> 16:11.320
You'll never change either!

16:34.650 --> 16:37.250
I'm on my way.

16:50.350 --> 16:51.870
Died just like that?

16:52.710 --> 16:54.770
A disappointment.

16:54.770 --> 16:57.110
He wasn't as skilled as the rumors say.

16:58.840 --> 17:01.210
Did he have any last words?

17:02.130 --> 17:03.490
...hear them.

17:04.470 --> 17:05.490
Eh?

17:06.040 --> 17:07.430
I couldn't hear them.

17:08.220 --> 17:10.570
Worthless.

17:14.380 --> 17:15.550
Let's head back.

17:16.080 --> 17:18.650
No. I'll stay here.

17:19.820 --> 17:22.210
I'd have taken either one, you know.

17:23.080 --> 17:26.420
His last words... or yours.

17:39.690 --> 17:43.200
<i>You'd better not betray my expectations.</i>

17:44.640 --> 17:46.270
Am I the same way?

18:00.470 --> 18:02.710
<i>I told you to get back.</i>

18:03.260 --> 18:05.110
<i>Where are you right—</i>

18:05.110 --> 18:07.880
Sorry. Need some time to cool off.

18:07.880 --> 18:09.160
<i>Huh? Hey, wait—</i>

18:14.090 --> 18:16.540
<i>You'll never change either!</i>

18:18.350 --> 18:21.020
<i>I tried, for so long, not to think.</i>

18:23.460 --> 18:25.490
<i>Just doing as I was ordered.</i>

18:26.150 --> 18:27.490
<i>Killing.</i>

18:28.020 --> 18:29.500
<i>Killing.</i>

18:30.070 --> 18:31.500
<i>Killing.</i>

18:33.830 --> 18:35.150
<i>Killing.</i>

18:37.100 --> 18:38.450
<i>I...</i>

18:43.130 --> 18:45.420
Hey, damn it! What're you doing, dumbass?!

18:45.420 --> 18:46.810
Kazuki?

18:46.810 --> 18:48.520
There's no time. Get in!

18:48.890 --> 18:50.100
No, I—

18:50.100 --> 18:51.990
I don't wanna hear it!

18:54.990 --> 18:55.870
Where's Miri?

18:56.150 --> 18:57.350
Home.

18:57.350 --> 18:58.540
You left her there?

18:58.540 --> 19:00.020
No worries.

19:00.020 --> 19:02.270
But we're short on time, so I'm gunning it.

19:08.050 --> 19:09.530
How'd you know where I was?

19:09.530 --> 19:12.790
Did you forget who set up your phone?

19:13.890 --> 19:15.660
You're overprotective.

19:15.980 --> 19:19.250
Miri was upset that you wouldn't come home.

19:19.250 --> 19:21.300
You forced my hand, asshole.

19:22.550 --> 19:25.080
Miri asked all about you.

19:25.080 --> 19:28.110
It took me back to old times.

19:28.690 --> 19:29.810
Old times?

19:30.170 --> 19:35.280
When Kyu-chan first introduced us,
 you were such a mess.

19:35.280 --> 19:38.810
Your room was full of garbage, 
all your food was instant crap.

19:39.180 --> 19:44.700
Unshaven, ungroomed, living like 
a shut-in with dead zombie eyes.

19:44.700 --> 19:48.040
Of course, you've still got 
the shut-in part down...

19:50.090 --> 19:56.170
Like you were any better, acting like 
you'd caused all the world's misfortunes.

19:56.170 --> 19:59.650
You were a useless load at work early on, too.

19:59.650 --> 20:00.700
Huh?!

20:00.700 --> 20:04.200
You never said anything before now!

20:04.200 --> 20:05.450
You're right. I didn't.

20:06.010 --> 20:08.840
I didn't think saying it 
would change anything.

20:09.290 --> 20:11.180
You didn't matter much to me.

20:13.340 --> 20:17.350
But then you suddenly started cleaning.

20:21.900 --> 20:25.790
I couldn't stand watching 
you live like that.

20:37.000 --> 20:39.480
I wanted to tell you to back off.

20:39.480 --> 20:40.830
Yeah, I'll bet.

20:43.060 --> 20:44.390
But...

20:44.860 --> 20:46.640
It wasn't so bad.

20:46.640 --> 20:48.290
Yeah, I'll bet!

20:49.110 --> 20:50.890
Hey, Kazuki.

20:53.400 --> 20:56.330
You think we can change?

20:57.950 --> 20:59.440
Dunno!

21:03.830 --> 21:04.980
I'm ba—

21:13.360 --> 21:15.670
Oh, it was today.

21:16.030 --> 21:18.450
Miri, Rei's back.

21:20.260 --> 21:22.710
Miri helped with everything.

21:22.710 --> 21:24.380
All day long.

21:24.380 --> 21:28.220
<b>Happy Birthday</b>

21:25.520 --> 21:28.230
She wanted to make you happy.

21:32.550 --> 21:36.490
Oh, Papa Rei! Welcome home!

21:38.250 --> 21:41.690
Happy birthday to you...

21:42.200 --> 21:45.370
Happy birthday...

21:50.080 --> 21:52.270
Hey! You did it, Miri!

21:52.270 --> 21:53.020
He smiled!

21:57.210 --> 21:58.000
Go on.

21:58.640 --> 21:59.360
Sure.

22:00.170 --> 22:04.170
<b>Happy Birthday</b>

22:08.230 --> 22:10.040
Sorry, we're—

22:15.210 --> 22:17.660
A request for info from the boss.

22:18.400 --> 22:21.360
The organization trusts you.

22:30.490 --> 22:35.540
<i>The scenery never changes and 
every day is full of surprises</i>

22:35.540 --> 22:40.000
<i>But those are the best parts</i>

22:40.000 --> 22:44.760
<i>Wrapped around your finger 
and going in circles</i>

22:45.010 --> 22:49.640
<i>These days are dizzying yet endearing</i>

22:49.840 --> 22:54.180
<i>On your restless nights, 
I softly whisper a lullaby</i>

22:54.180 --> 22:58.940
<i>And stroke your hair to the 
rhythm of your breathing</i>

22:59.400 --> 23:03.520
<i>I just want these days to 
continue as long as possible</i>

23:03.520 --> 23:08.530
<i>Even if it's just a day</i>

23:09.320 --> 23:14.240
<i>I chased after you as you ran barefoot</i>

23:14.240 --> 23:18.460
<i>Maybe one day, you'll surpass me, ah</i>

23:18.460 --> 23:23.130
<i>I wonder what tomorrow's going to be like</i>

23:23.130 --> 23:28.050
<i>Why don't we walk together?</i>

23:28.050 --> 23:32.800
<i>This will always be our place to come home to</i>

23:33.300 --> 23:37.600
<i>And it'll shine down on our sadness</i>

23:37.600 --> 23:42.270
<i>That's all right, yeah, that's okay</i>

23:42.270 --> 23:47.190
<i>Let's try to share our love together</i>

23:47.190 --> 23:50.610
<i>Let the light always shine upon hope</i>

23:50.610 --> 23:57.120
<i>When the future is unpredictable</i>
